# Content Tracker (@piselliii)

Personal Next.js app for X content discipline. **Not MoveMatch / not ffl-moves.**

## Product

- 8 habit types with weekly norms (hot topic, meme, useful, bait, provocative, strategic QT, builder, meta reach)
- Done / − / + / log with tweet URL + views/likes
- Ideas backlog, localStorage, Export/Backup, **Copy for Jarvis** JSON
- Live: content-tracker-vert.vercel.app · Repo: github.com/Piselli/content-traker

## Stack

Next.js 16 App Router · TypeScript · Tailwind · `public/tracker-data.json` synced on load + localStorage

## Key files

- `public/tracker-data.json` — **source of truth** agent commits after user sends tweet data
- `src/lib/norms.ts` — weekly targets
- `src/lib/analysis.ts` — insights, next slot, bucket mix
- `src/hooks/useTracker.ts` — state + repo merge
- `src/components/Dashboard.tsx` — main UI
- `JARVIS.md` — X content strategy (PICK, DRAFT, norms)

## Logging workflow (when user sends screenshot + URL)

User does **not** need to click Done on site if agent handles logging.

| When | User sends | Agent does |
|------|------------|------------|
| Right after post | screenshot + URL (+ «опублікував» optional) | Classify `type` + `traits` + `slot` + `bucket` → update `public/tracker-data.json` → **commit + push** (no ask) |
| ~3h later | screenshot + URL | Update metrics (`ageHours`, views, likes, replies) → commit + push |
| ~24h later | screenshot + URL | Update metrics; previous check-in saved in `snapshots` |

- **Primary `type`** = norm progress (Done). **`traits[]`** = combo coverage — badges + analytics, not norms
- Same tweet URL = update existing log, do not duplicate.
- Communicate analysis to user **in Ukrainian**. App UI stays English.
- User consults in chat before posting → agent already knows classification when they say «опублікував».

## Code conventions

- Minimal scope; no over-engineering
- Keep UI dark, simple, mobile-friendly
- No auth/API unless user asks
- Ukrainian OK in chat; app UI in English

